<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<GenerateModel xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="generateMetaModel_Module.xsd">
    <PythonExport
        Father="ViewProviderPy"
        Name="ViewProviderDocumentObjectPy"
        Twin="ViewProviderDocumentObject"
        TwinPointer="ViewProviderDocumentObject"
        Include="Gui/ViewProviderDocumentObject.h"
        Namespace="Gui"
        FatherInclude="Gui/ViewProviderPy.h"
        FatherNamespace="Gui">
        <Documentation>
            <Author Licence="LGPL" Name="Werner Mayer" EMail="wmayer@users.sourceforge.net" />
            <UserDocu>This is the ViewProvider base class</UserDocu>
        </Documentation>
        <Methode Name="update">
            <Documentation>
                <UserDocu>Update the view representation of the object</UserDocu>
            </Documentation>
            <Sandbox tier="call"/>
        </Methode>
        <Methode Name="showValueDiff" Keyword="true">
            <Documentation>
                <UserDocu>showValueDiff(prop, a='', b='', position=1.0, differencesOnly=False, mode='') -> bool

Show over the object how property 'prop' differs between two values the
transaction log holds, each by its ref; an empty ref is the value the object has
now. 'position' is where between the two, 0 at a and 1 at b. 'mode' is which of
the ways the view provider has to show it: of a shape 'faces', what became of
each face, or 'material', the solid only one of the two has. False where this
view provider shows no such thing, or the log does not hold a value.</UserDocu>
            </Documentation>
        </Methode>
        <Methode Name="hideValueDiff">
            <Documentation>
                <UserDocu>hideValueDiff() -- take away what showValueDiff() shows</UserDocu>
            </Documentation>
        </Methode>
        <Methode Name="getValueDiff">
            <Documentation>
                <UserDocu>getValueDiff() -> dict

What showValueDiff() shows now, as numbers by name -- a whole number an int, any
other a float; empty where nothing is.</UserDocu>
            </Documentation>
        </Methode>
		<Methode Name="isShowable">
			<Documentation>
				<UserDocu>isShowable(refresh=False) -- Check if the view object is showable</UserDocu>
			</Documentation>
		</Methode>
        <Attribute Name="Object">
            <Documentation>
                <UserDocu>Set/Get the associated data object</UserDocu>
            </Documentation>
            <Parameter Name="Object" Type="Object" />
            <Sandbox tier="handle"/>
        </Attribute>
        <Attribute Name="ForceUpdate">
            <Documentation>
                <UserDocu>Reference count to force update visual</UserDocu>
            </Documentation>
            <Parameter Name="ForceUpdate" Type="Boolean" />
        </Attribute>
        <Attribute Name="ClaimedChildren" ReadOnly="true">
            <Documentation>
                <UserDocu>Obtain claimed child view objects</UserDocu>
            </Documentation>
            <Parameter Name="ClaimedChildren" Type="List" />
        </Attribute>
        <Attribute Name="ClaimedBy" ReadOnly="true">
            <Documentation>
                <UserDocu>Obtain all parent view objects that claim this view object</UserDocu>
            </Documentation>
            <Parameter Name="ClaimedBy" Type="List" />
        </Attribute>
        <Attribute Name="Document" ReadOnly="true">
            <Documentation>
                <UserDocu>Return the document the view provider is part of</UserDocu>
            </Documentation>
            <Parameter Name="Document" Type="Object" />
        </Attribute>
    </PythonExport>
</GenerateModel>
